## Scoring Algorithm

The overall firmware risk is a **weighted average** of 5 categories:

| Category | Weight | Key Inputs |
|----------|--------|------------|
| Jailbreak | 25% | Applicable jailbreak tools, checkm8 hardware status |
| Kernel | 30% | Unpatched kernel CVEs, binary ASLR/PIE status |
| Userland | 15% | Sandbox escapes, TCC bypasses, entitlement audit, banned APIs |
| Injection | 15% | Signing bypasses, PIE gaps, bootrom access |
| Malware | 15% | Known spyware CVEs, WebKit RCEs, kernel chain potential |

Each category score is capped at 5-95% to prevent absolute zero/max claims.

